As a therapist,
I want to initiate a child's learning session directly from the therapist web portal,
so that I can facilitate in-clinic or supervised sessions without requiring the parent to be present or logged in.

Background

The Cognitivebotics learning session (where a child works through their ILP's Learning Objectives) currently runs on the mobile/caregiver app. 

It does not run in the browser. Therapists who want to run a session in clinic today must use the parent's login credentials or ask the parent to start the session remotely — both are friction-heavy.

This story surfaces a "Start session" entry point in three locations on the therapist portal. In all three cases, the action does not start a session in-browser; it redirects the therapist to open the Parent app automatically or download the app if it does not exist. 

Acceptance Criteria

Plan Status Gate (applies to all three entry points)

"Start session" is disabled (visible but not clickable) for any child whose plan status is "No plan" or "Plan ended".

When a therapist hovers over a disabled "Start session" control, a tooltip appears explaining why: "Assign an active plan before starting a session."

"Start session" is enabled for children with plan status: On track, Limited progress, or Plan ending.

Entry Point 1 — Dashboard: Recently Active Children List

The dashboard displays a recently active children list. Each child row has a play button  displayed on the left side of the row.

When a therapist hovers over the play button for a child with an active plan, a tooltip reading "Start session" appears.

Clicking the play button for an eligible child opens the redirect modal (see Redirect Modal Behaviour ).

The play button is visible only for children explicitly assigned to the logged-in therapist. Children not on the therapist's caseload do not show a play button.

Entry Point 2 — Children Tab: Child List Row Action Menu

The Children tab displays a list of children. Each row has a 3-dot menu (⋮) on the right.

Clicking the ⋮ menu on a child row reveals exactly two options: "Start session" and "Remove child".

"Start session" in the ⋮ menu is disabled (greyed out, not clickable) for children with "No plan" or "Plan ended" status, per AC-1 and AC-2.

Clicking an enabled "Start session" from the ⋮ menu opens the redirect modal (see Redirect Modal Behaviour below).

The ⋮ menu is visible only for children explicitly assigned to the logged-in therapist.

The Children tab child list displays the following fields per row: Child name, Therapist(s) assigned, Last played date, Objectives mastered (shown as a progress bar), and Plan status badge. Plan status badges are: On track, Limited progress, Plan ending, Plan ended, No plan.

Entry Point 3 — Individual Child Learning Plan Page

The individual child's Learning Plan page has a "Start session" button in the top-right corner of the page, displayed alongside the "Update Plan" button.

The "Start session" button is disabled (per AC-1 and AC-2) if the child's plan status is "No plan" or "Plan ended".

Clicking an enabled "Start session" from the Learning Plan page opens the redirect modal (see Redirect Modal Behaviour below).

The "Start session" button on this page is visible only if the logged-in therapist is explicitly assigned to the child.

Redirect Modal Behaviour

On a mobile device (iOS or Android): The primary button reads "Continue in App", determined by the device OS. The button uses a universal link: if the Cognitivebotics mobile app is already installed, it opens the app directly; if not, it opens the relevant store listing. 

On a desktop browser (macOS or Windows): In place of the store button, the modal displays a QR code. Scanning the QR code with a phone takes the therapist to the correct store for their phone's OS (iOS App Store or Google Play). A caption below the QR code reads: "Scan with your phone or tablet to open the app."

Clicking "Cancel" closes the modal. The therapist is returned to the exact view they were on before the modal appeared, with no state change.

The modal does not initiate a session, create a session record, or write any data. It is a redirect-only interaction.

