Session Attribution

When a therapist logs into the Cognitivebotics mobile app using their therapist credentials and starts a session, the system records the session initiator as "Therapist" in the session record.

When a parent/caregiver logs into the mobile app and starts a session, the system records the session initiator as "Parent".

The session record's initiator field must store at least two values: "Therapist" and "Parent". The field must be stored on the session record in the backend and be queryable. It is the data foundation for a downstream reporting story (not surfaced in any existing UI view in this story).

Session attribution is determined by the account type used to log into the mobile app at the time of session start — not by who clicked "Start session" on the web portal.

Access Control

A therapist can only see and interact with "Start session" controls for children who are explicitly assigned to them in the system.

A therapist navigating directly to a child's Learning Plan page for a child not on their caseload must not see the "Start session" button on that page.

If a therapist somehow triggers the "Start session" action for an unassigned child (e.g., via direct URL manipulation), the system must return an authorization error and not open the modal or write any data.

